00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:13.520
OK. How do I increase my understanding&nbsp;
of AI beyond off-the-shelf packages?&nbsp;

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:19.160
I've got the answer to that one: you have to&nbsp;
build things. I mean many of the most capable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:27.160
AI practitioners just put effort into building&nbsp;
things for themselves, reimplementing things.&nbsp;

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:33.360
You know, one great example of that 
is the Stanford PhD grad Andrej Karpathy.&nbsp;

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:38.960
So Andrej has had a career, first working&nbsp;
at Tesla and now he's back at OpenAI,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:44.040
but you know he's also just a weekend&nbsp;
hacker who likes to build things.&nbsp;

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:48.600
And the reality is that just by building&nbsp;
things for yourself from scratch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:54.000
even if they replicate something that someone&nbsp;
has done or a big framework from a tech company,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:59.360
you just learn so much and that's&nbsp;
always a great exercise to work through.&nbsp;

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:05.480
OK, what are some promising&nbsp;
new career paths within AI?&nbsp;

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:13.280
So there are a lot, right. We're still at a stage&nbsp;
in which there's just a huge shortage of 

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:18.520
machine learning engineers and a huge shortage of people&nbsp;
with a good understanding of neural networks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:23.520
natural language processing and&nbsp;
robotics and related technologies.&nbsp;

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:29.360
So if you get good skills in these areas&nbsp;
there are all sorts of things that you can do.&nbsp;

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:37.000
Every kind of industry, whether you're thinking&nbsp;
the car industry, people in banking and finance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:43.400
people in construction, people who would like to&nbsp;
automate mining or agriculture, anywhere you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:51.880
look there are ways that you could use artificial&nbsp;
intelligence to reinvent different Industries.&nbsp;

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:58.720
OK, I've completed the basics of machine learning&nbsp;
and deep learning, what should I learn next?&nbsp;

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:03.000
I don't think that's a question&nbsp;
that has a one-size-fits-all answer.&nbsp;

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:08.800
One answer is find a project that's something that&nbsp;
you're really interested in. It could be something&nbsp;&nbsp;at work

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:14.640
or it could just be something that's&nbsp;completely 
an interest of yours as a hobbyist&nbsp;thing. 

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:22.920
So spending more time actually building an&nbsp;
AI application from beginning to end is still a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:28.840
huge further learning exercise after doing one&nbsp;
or two of our classes. But there are lots of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:33.560
other great classes you could do and I think&nbsp;
at that point it depends more on what you're&nbsp;interested in.&nbsp;

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:39.560
[Music]

